{
  "_README": [
    "Both watchers read this file -- edit here to tune what gets alerted.",
    "",
    "Two tiers, because the two sources need different strictness:",
    "  core_cs          -- tight, software/CS-specific terms. Used ALONE against",
    "                      SimplifyJobs, a 14k-listing aggregator that also carries",
    "                      hardware, quant-trading-desk and non-technical reqs.",
    "  broad_engineering -- extra general terms, added ON TOP of core only for the",
    "                      curated company boards in ats_config.json. Every company",
    "                      there is already a software company, so any engineering",
    "                      intern on those boards is worth seeing.",
    "",
    "exclude -- dropped from both, even on a keyword hit. For a CS list this is",
    "          doing more work than the tiers are: tech-company boards are full of",
    "          Sales Engineer / Solutions Engineer / Support Engineer reqs that hit",
    "          'engineer' in the broad tier but are not software roles.",
    "us_canada_only -- drop postings whose location is clearly overseas.",
    "",
    "Terms match as whole words, case-insensitive, so 'ml' won't hit 'html'.",
    "",
    "Scope is Summer 2027 specifically -- Spring/Winter 2027 titles are dropped by",
    "check_company_boards.py's SPRING_RE / WINTER_RE even when 2027 also appears",
    "(Notion and Databricks both post paired Winter/Summer 2027 reqs).",
    "",
    "Keep bare generic words OUT of core_cs -- it runs against an aggregator with",
    "no company-level filtering, so 'engineer', 'systems' or a bare 'ai' drag in",
    "hardware, civil and sales reqs. Such words belong in broad_engineering, or as",
    "a qualified compound phrase in core (e.g. 'ai engineer' / 'systems software')."
  ],
