  "_category_README": [
    "Discord alerts stay scoped to all of core_robotics/broad_engineering above",
    "(humanoid, drones, warehouse arms included) -- that breadth is deliberate,",
    "it's the discovery net. The write-back to data/job_log.jsonl now keeps",
    "everything that net catches too (not just AV), but tags every record with",
    "a sub-category so a later analysis can compare skill demand across",
    "robotics sub-fields instead of only seeing an undifferentiated pile.",
    "",
    "company_categories is a manually curated split of ats_config.json's 44",
    "companies -- check it when a new company is added there. For a company",
    "NOT in that map (every SimplifyJobs entry, since ats_config.json only",
    "covers the board-watcher's 44), category_terms is tried in the listed",
    "order (av first) against the title+company; first match wins. Nothing",
    "matching falls back to 'general_robotics_other'. See classify_job() in",
    "job_store.py."
  ],
